      "raw_time": false,
      "body": "I'm now thinking about going through the fine-tune template notebook, and slowly adapting it to my filament chirality idea. First of all, I want to think about how can I help Surya find the filament I'm discussing. Am I passing in the hemisphere or could I also pass in the coordinates of the filament identified in the catalog? Or can I simply just tell Surya nothing and then it will try to learn itself. In all, I know my low number of 45 events has high error but I want to understand the possibilities."
