      "time": 1789583758.7477577,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "That's a reasonable sequencing \u2014 get the full pipeline (data alignment, LoRA, training loop, metrics) working end-to-end on something simple before touching patch-embed weights for a new channel. The main tradeoff: with 45 samples and a full 4096\u00d74096 search space, don't over-read the resulting accuracy as a real ceiling on the full-disk approach \u2014 it's more useful as a pipeline sanity check than a meaningful chirality number, since the model has little chance to reliably find the filament without a location cue at that sample size.",
      "id": "6ebdb8f7-9c31-4f36-9d75-962dfff39ff8",
      "raw_time": false
    },
