      "sender": "jupyter-ai-personas::jupyter_ai_acp_client::ClaudeAcpPersona",
      "raw_time": false,
      "type": "msg",
      "body": "Mostly yes, but I found one thing that would bite you silently: `load_pretrained_weights()` in `utils.py:383` only keeps checkpoint keys whose **shape matches exactly** \u2014 mismatches are dropped outright, not partially merged. So bumping `in_channels` from 13\u219214 wouldn't zero-init just the new channel like I described; it would drop the *entire* `patch_embed.proj` weight back to random init, throwing away the pretrained patch embedding on all 13 real channels too, silently (no error, just a lower \"Loaded N/M\" count in the printout).\n\nThe retrofit is still moderate-not-hard, but it's three real pieces of work, not one: (1) get actual pixel/heliographic coordinates into your catalog \u2014 not there yet, (2) render the heatmap channel in the dataset and concatenate it, and (3) add a small shape-aware patch to `load_pretrained_weights` (or a special case before it) that pads the checkpoint's conv weight with a zero-initialized 14th-channel slice before the shape check, so you don't lose the pretrained embedding. None of that touches the LoRA/head code you'll already have working. Want me to sketch that patch now, or hold it until you're actually ready to add the channel?"
    },
