      "mentions": [],
      "body": "The clarifying-question tool isn't available in this session, so let me just ask directly:\n\n1. **Trainable baseline** (`models/simple_baseline.py`) is still an unmodified copy of the flare-regression linear model. Your `1_baseline_filament.ipynb` already has two solid non-trainable baselines (coin-flip Monte Carlo + leave-one-out calibrated Martin's Rule). Do you want me to also adapt this trainable linear baseline for chirality (keeps the `--train_baseline` flag working), or drop it and rely on the two baselines you already have?\n\n2. **Classification metrics** (`metrics/template_metrics.py` currently reports MSE/RRSE for regression) \u2014 for `train_metrics`/`val_metrics`, is plain binary accuracy enough, or do you also want balanced accuracy tracked in case the 45 events end up skewed by chirality/hemisphere?",
